## 1. Versions (verified live 2026-11-19)
- astro `latest` on npm: **7.4.13** (engines: node >=22.23.4, npm >=9.6.5, pnpm >=7.1.0)
- Astro 6.0 — released **2026-03-10** (astro.build/blog/astro-6/): CSP stable, Fonts API stable, Live Content Collections (`defineLiveCollection`), redesigned `astro dev` (Vite Environment API), breaking: Node 22+, Vite 7, Shiki 4, **Zod 4 — import `z` from `astro/zod`, no longer from `astro:content`**.
- Astro 7.0 — released **2026-06-22** (astro.build/blog/astro-7/): Vite 8 + Rolldown (Rust bundler), Rust `.astro` compiler (stricter: unclosed tags/unterminated attributes now ERROR), Rust markdown pipeline "Sätteri" (GFM/smart punctuation/heading IDs built in, replaces unified), Advanced Routing via `src/fetch.ts` (fetch-handler pattern, Hono-compatible), route caching stabilized (`cache`/`routeRules` moved out of `experimental`), builds 15–61% faster. 7.1 (2026-07-16): CSP `script-src-elem/attr`, `style-src-elem/attr`. 7.4 (2026-10-15): `--timings`, separate build/runtime image services, experimental parallel prerendering.
- Install: `npm create astro@latest` or `npm i astro@^7.4.13`. @astrojs/sitemap **3.7.6**. @astrojs/netlify **8.2.14** (if ever needed for staticHeaders).

## 2. i18n — French at root, /en/, no redirect, no detection
```js
// astro.config.mjs
import { defineConfig } from 'astro/config';
export default defineConfig({
  site: 'https://www.example.fr',
  i18n: {
    locales: ['fr', 'en'],
    defaultLocale: 'fr',
    routing: {
      prefixDefaultLocale: false, // default — FR has NO /fr prefix
    },
  },
});
```
File layout: `src/pages/index.astro` → `/` (French); `src/pages/en/index.astro` → `/en/`. With `prefixDefaultLocale: false` there is **no redirect of any kind** and Astro performs **no browser-language detection ever** (that's not a feature of Astro i18n; `redirectToDefaultLocale` only exists for the `prefixDefaultLocale: true` mode, default true there). `routing: "manual"` disables the i18n middleware entirely — unnecessary here. Do not configure `fallback` (it generates redirects between locales).

## 3. Content collections (Content Layer, current API)
```ts
// src/content.config.ts
import { defineCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { glob } from 'astro/loaders';
import { z } from 'astro/zod'; // Zod 4 — NOT from 'astro:content' since Astro 6

const projects = defineCollection({
  loader: glob({ pattern: '**/*.md', base: './src/content/projects' }),
  schema: ({ image }) =>
    z.object({
      title: z.string(),
      description: z.string(),
      pubDate: z.coerce.date(),
      cover: image(),          // validates ./cover.jpg colocated next to the .md
      coverAlt: z.string(),
    }),
});
export const collections = { projects };
```
Frontmatter: `cover: ./cover.jpg` (relative to the markdown file). `image()` resolves it to image metadata usable directly in `<Image src={entry.data.cover} ...>`. Use `getCollection('projects', ({ data }) => import.meta.env.PROD ? !data.draft : true)` for draft filtering.

## 4. astro:assets
- Default service: Sharp (`astro/assets/services/sharp`). **Every processed output (Image/Picture/getImage) is re-encoded by Sharp, which strips ALL metadata — EXIF, GPS, ICC.** Confirmed: roadmap discussion withastro/roadmap#1251 ("Allow preserving image metadata") exists precisely because stripping is unconditional; the only way to KEEP metadata is a custom image service calling `.keepMetadata()`. Good for privacy — nothing to configure.
- **Caveat: files in `public/` and any original asset you link directly are copied byte-for-byte — EXIF/GPS NOT stripped.** Run exiftool on anything in public/ (incl. demo assets).
- Default output format: `.webp` (Image component). AVIF: `<Picture src={img} formats={['avif','webp']} alt="..." />` (Picture `formats` default is `['webp']`; original format is the fallback).
- srcset: set `layout` prop (`constrained` | `full-width` | `fixed` | `none`) → Astro auto-generates `srcset` + `sizes`; or set globally `image: { layout: 'constrained', responsiveStyles: true }` in config (stable since 5.10). Manual control: `widths={[400, 800, 1200]}` or `densities={[1.5, 2]}`.

## 5. Strict CSP / zero inline
What Astro emits inline by default: (a) component `<style>` is bundled to external CSS, BUT `build.inlineStylesheets` default `'auto'` inlines stylesheets smaller than `vite.build.assetsInlineLimit` (4kb) as `<style>` tags; (b) `<script>` in components become external `type="module"` files, BUT "if the script is small enough, Astro will inline it directly into the HTML".

Option A — zero inline anything, plain `script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'` header at the host:
```js
export default defineConfig({
  build: { inlineStylesheets: 'never' },
  vite: { build: { assetsInlineLimit: 0 } }, // also stops small-script inlining
});
```
(avoid `is:inline`/`define:vars` on style/script, and `<style>` in markdown).

Option B — built-in hash-based CSP, STABLE since 6.0 (`security.csp`, formerly `experimental.csp` in 5.9):
```js
export default defineConfig({
  security: {
    csp: {
      algorithm: 'SHA-256', // default; also SHA-384/SHA-512
      directives: [
        "default-src 'self'",
        "img-src 'self' data:",
        "font-src 'self'",
        "frame-ancestors 'none'", // NOTE: ignored in <meta> delivery — set at host
      ],
      styleDirective: { resources: ["'self'"] },   // hashes: [] for extra manual hashes
      scriptDirective: { resources: ["'self'"], strictDynamic: false },
    },
  },
});
```
Astro hashes all its bundled/inlined scripts and styles at build time and injects `<meta http-equiv="content-security-policy">` into each static page. 7.1 added support for `script-src-elem/attr` and `style-src-elem/attr`. Limitation: `<meta>` CSP cannot carry `frame-ancestors`, `report-uri`, `sandbox` — for a pure-static no-adapter build, keep those (and ideally the whole CSP) in real HTTP headers at the host. If hosting on Netlify/Vercel, the adapters (@astrojs/netlify 8.2.14) now have a **stable `staticHeaders: true`** option that writes the computed CSP as real response headers for prerendered pages instead of the meta tag:
```js
adapter: netlify({ staticHeaders: true })  // with security: { csp: true }
```
Recommended for this portfolio: Option A (deterministic, header-set-once at host) — hashes change on every content edit otherwise. Note: static demo pages under `public/demos/<slug>/` are NOT processed by Astro, so their inline scripts are NOT hashed — either make demos inline-free too or scope a per-path CSP header at the host.

## 6. Sitemap with hreflang
```js
import sitemap from '@astrojs/sitemap';
export default defineConfig({
  site: 'https://www.example.fr', // required by the integration
  integrations: [
    sitemap({
      i18n: {
        defaultLocale: 'fr',
        locales: { fr: 'fr-FR', en: 'en-US' },
      },
      // filter: (page) => !page.includes('/styleguide'),
    }),
  ],
});
```
Emits `<xhtml:link rel="alternate" hreflang="fr-FR" href=".../"/>` + `hreflang="en-US" href=".../en/"` pairs for each page. The sitemap's `i18n` block is its own config — it is NOT auto-derived from `defineConfig({ i18n })`. Keys of `locales` must match the path prefixes ('fr' = unprefixed default).

## 7. Fonts — Fonts API is STABLE (since 6.0), top-level `fonts` key
```js
import { defineConfig, fontProviders } from 'astro/config';
export default defineConfig({
  fonts: [{
    provider: fontProviders.local(),
    name: 'Inter',
    cssVariable: '--font-inter',
    options: {
      variants: [
        { src: ['./src/assets/fonts/inter-latin-400.woff2'], weight: 400, style: 'normal' },
        { src: ['./src/assets/fonts/inter-latin-700.woff2'], weight: 700, style: 'normal' },
      ],
    },
  }],
});
```
```astro
---
import { Font } from 'astro:assets';
---
<head><Font cssVariable="--font-inter" preload /></head>
<style> body { font-family: var(--font-inter); } </style>
```
Files are copied to `_astro/fonts/` (hashed, year-long immutable caching), preload links added, and optimized fallback fonts auto-generated (size-adjusted metrics → less CLS); customize/disable via `fallbacks`. Even remote providers (`fontProviders.google()`) are downloaded at build and self-hosted — no runtime third-party request, which satisfies CNIL doctrine on Google Fonts. Plain `@font-face` in a global CSS + files in `public/fonts/` still works but you lose hashing/caching/fallback generation and must hand-write preload links. Note the syntax changed from the 5.x experimental era (`provider: "local"`, top-level `variants`) to stable (`fontProviders.local()`, `options.variants`) — old snippets fail.

## 8. Excluding /styleguide from production builds
No built-in option (withastro/roadmap discussion #1188 still open). Two working patterns:

A) Rest-param route + conditional getStaticPaths (pure static, env-based):
```astro
---
// src/pages/styleguide/[...index].astro  → serves /styleguide/ in dev only
export function getStaticPaths() {
  if (import.meta.env.PROD) return [];          // not built in `astro build`
  return [{ params: { index: undefined } }];
}
---
<h1>Styleguide</h1>
```
B) Dev-only injected route via a 5-line integration (page lives outside src/pages):
```js
// astro.config.mjs
const devPages = () => ({
  name: 'dev-pages',
  hooks: {
    'astro:config:setup': ({ command, injectRoute }) => {
      if (command === 'dev') {
        injectRoute({ pattern: '/styleguide', entrypoint: './src/dev-pages/styleguide.astro' });
      }
    },
  },
});
export default defineConfig({ integrations: [devPages()] });
```
Variant: gate on `process.env.SHOW_STYLEGUIDE === 'true'` instead of `command` for build-time env control. Also remember the `_` prefix trick (`src/pages/_drafts/...` is never routed) and the sitemap `filter` option if the page ships but must stay out of the sitemap.
